          "passage_id": "e8b83857d216e267ad769ac29bdd205a9038601458cf8d4da6e7e73d4b197674",
          "evidence_quote": "Violation may result in rejected pull requests, blocked releases, package quarantine, revocation of repository or CI\n\nprivileges, mandatory remediation, disciplinary action up to and including termination, contractual remedies for\nsuppliers, and legal escalation where licensing or IP obligations are breached. Security may require immediate\n\nremoval of a component without waiting for a normal release window when active exploitation or malicious\n\nsupply-chain activity is suspected.\n\nWhere a violation creates active risk, protective action may occur before disciplinary or contractual review is complete.\n\nEnforcement decisions will consider intent, recurrence, severity, impact, legal duties, and whether the individual\n\npromptly reported the issue and cooperated with remediation.",
